l is for\n                values you compute. Global is shared.\n                * Read: `read({\"kind\":\"variable\",\"id\":\"<name>\"})` searches vault→local→global.\n                  Or pass `scope=\"<scope>\"` to target one scope.\n                * Write: `write({\"kind\":\"variable\",\"id\":\"<name>\"}, {\"value\": <v>}, scope=\"<scope>\")`.\n                * Search: `search(query, kind=\"variable\")` lists matching variables across\n                  scopes; pass `query=\"\"` to list every variable in the workspace.\n- `spec`      — schema document (OpenAPI / GraphQL SDL / Protobuf). `read` it to get\n                the full schema directly (paths, methods, auth, fields are inline in\n                its `document`). Note: the spec documents what's *published*; the live\n                API may have undocumented behavior you'll only see by calling it.\n- `handle`    — long-running execution token (rare in v0.1).\n\n# How to work\n\nYou have a real goal, not a script — decide your own approach. In general: get your\nbearings (what entities, specs, and variables exist?), read the schema and any\nrelevant response bodies, `execute` the API calls you need (inline `request={...}` is\nthe normal one-step way), and persist values you'll need again. There's no fixed\nnumber of steps; do what the task needs and stop.\n\nWhen something doesn't behave as expected (a 4xx/5xx, an empty body, a surprising\nshape), **read the response and the spec to understand WHY before you retry or move\non.** Diagnosing a failure is part of doing the job well; blind retrying or guessing\nis not. Verify your work actually landed (re-read what you stored, confirm a call\nreturned what you needed) rather than assuming it did.\n\n# Finishing\n\n- Stop calling tools when the task is genuinely done. Calling no tool ends the trial.\n- Don't over-act, under-act, or claim you did something you didn't.\n- Use `clarify` only if the task is genuinely ambiguous AFTER you've inventoried the\n  workspace; use `report_blocked` only once you've established (via tool calls) that\n  the task can't be done. Both terminate the trial — choose carefully.\n\n\n\nYou are a helpful assistant attempting to submit the best possible answer. You have several tools available to help with finding the answer. You will see the result of tool calls right after sending the message. If you need to perform multiple actions, you can always send more messages with additional tool calls. Do some reasoning before your actions, describing what tool calls you are going to use and how they fit into your plan.\n"},{"role":"user","content":"Bearer's cached. Need to pin one more marker for the reconcile sheet, and it has to come off the audit feed /v3/audit-events specifically — it's the only v3 feed carrying a per-event kind field. Walk every page (Link rel=next until it's gone, NOT the deprecated v2 loop) and find the dev-C event — there's exactly ONE dev-C row across the whole feed. Save its canonical event id into a variable so the reconcile job can anchor dev-C on the audit side. Don't grab any of the dev-A or dev-B rows, and don't pull dev-C off /v3/checkins or /v3/pings — those have no kind field and a different dev-C id.\n\nWhen you have finished, report your final answer as a single JSON object inside a ```json code block, with exactly these field(s): `dev_c_event_id`. Use the exact field name(s) shown, and put each requested value as that field's value."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"reasoning","reasoning":"gAAAAABqQ0ylxPvt-mstag-VNeSz5shqRPKME32ZpP3f3WpexIH6Mt8c5TVeNbf-ZAyxJ9lBRptkXTYFfpZKeFlk1h_eN-tMX8BHDS8K5nN9wdR01k7B3u4FFFgVvIS1RR6wIGom8dRW-nj4buaguQ7CN5-I-Jgfc3XtB_I0ipiy8GBwSIHbUgGXbWvSsR4Zn_fWVT5Lyt0DS86HLaHaCEpFcWZ-O4k-boWLyfbmKRHSDgsXspbVMZwoHQINAUXtQFpF5uA_NKyTMqitiOoTSAgfqVZwepYNcMxx00uJo6uNnXFavn4KYTyNq6TAqioGcNYPVL2jwJeqMumBkKWV4wRkzRYkzC9NCVFKWBiJbXvAr3y6B7ElUTItemB0f1J5qcUs2Dg2X_CVTcKpB6xxb_cmxXN14e1dmrvBQd3-Sp7w1AATEL8duJTdipKkcp6-t_U0AS3N-yLXYFhu5ah4GNow